From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: don't dereference a missing xHCI hcd on suspend

The xHCI platform device created by dwc3 outlives its driver: after
"echo xhci-hcd.N.auto > /sys/bus/platform/drivers/xhci-hcd/unbind" it has no
driver data. With wakeup-source set on the glue, system suspend then reaches
dwc3_qcom_read_usb2_speed(), which dereferences hcd->self.root_hub with a
NULL hcd. On the ROG Phone 5 (oops=panic) this reset the phone at the first
s2idle after a suspend hook had unbound the xHCI (2026-09-29 17:29). Report
an unknown speed instead. Both the legacy and the flattened glue have the
code. Found by the ROG5 night review (USB agent).

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c	2026-09-30 03:27:24.424661081 +0200
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c	2026-09-30 03:27:32.073981862 +0200
@@ -327,6 +327,12 @@
 	 * FIXME: Fix this layering violation.
 	 */
 	hcd = platform_get_drvdata(dwc->xhci);
+	/*
+	 * The xHCI platform device outlives its driver: with xhci-hcd unbound
+	 * (sysfs unbind) there is no hcd, and system suspend used to oops here.
+	 */
+	if (!hcd)
+		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
 	udev = usb_hub_find_child(hcd->self.root_hub, port_index + 1);
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c	2026-09-30 03:27:24.431737571 +0200
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c	2026-09-30 03:27:32.074072073 +0200
@@ -239,6 +239,12 @@
 	 * FIXME: Fix this layering violation.
 	 */
 	hcd = platform_get_drvdata(dwc->xhci);
+	/*
+	 * The xHCI platform device outlives its driver: with xhci-hcd unbound
+	 * (sysfs unbind) there is no hcd, and system suspend used to oops here.
+	 */
+	if (!hcd)
+		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
 	udev = usb_hub_find_child(hcd->self.root_hub, port_index + 1);
